"The postoperative pathology is reassuring regarding local disease, as the surgical pathology report documented \"surgical margins were negative\" and \"the seminal vesicles were not invaded.\" The surgical pathology also noted \"no lymph nodes were removed.\" Conversely, the preoperative findings included a Gleason 4+3 (ISUP grade group 4) and perineural invasion noted in the biopsy report. The absence of documented nodal sampling means that the pNx status does not establish node-negative disease, which widens the uncertainty regarding regional control. The prognosis is tempered by the documented perineural invasion, despite negative margins and no seminal vesicle invasion. Postoperative PSA is not recorded, meaning biochemical recurrence cannot be assessed. Information regarding postoperative PSA and its subsequent trajectory is crucial for revising the prognosis. The fixed estimated horizon is 51.41 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 33.42–69.40 months; its coverage has not been validated."
